1 Hotfix 1\n- Renamed class levels to Mastery to avoid confusion\n- Fixed an issue which was preventing mastery gains from showing up in the UI (you were earning mastery, but you had to restart the game to see the changes)\n- Made several other UI fixes involving mastery", "created_date": 1778882856, "id": "27242936615290900", "version": "1.0.11", "version_code": 44, "release_status": "RELEASED", "status": "APPROVED", "binary_test_results": {"nodes": []}, "obb_binary": null, "asset_files": {"count": 0}, "debug_symbols": {"count": 0}, "__isAppBinaryWithFileAsset": "AndroidBinary"}, {"__typename": "AndroidBinary", "__isAppBinary": "AndroidBinary", "binary_application": {"__typename": "Application", "id": "25080401538211096", "is_concept": false, "latest_released_binary": {"__typename": "AndroidBinary", "id": "27255560764028485"}, "release_status": "RELEASED"}, "binary_release_channels": {"nodes": [{"channel_name": "LIVE", "id": "25740082985581976"}]}, "change_log": "Patch 1.0.11 Notes\n\nNew Features:\n- Added 4 new unlockable signature spells: Burning Bow, Purging Whip, Giant's Hammer, and Leeching Link!\n- Players can now toggle crouching by pressing down on the right joystick. The alternative way of activating Fly is now the B button\n- Added an announcement scroll to the Hub\n- Added tournaments and tournament leaderboards! The first Duel tournament starts on 5/16!\n\nBalancing Changes:\n- Reduced golem damage vs players. Increased siege and melee golem damage vs towers\n- Reduced difficulty of last two Gauntlet levels slightly\n- Reduced Daze duration for the default Hammer to 3 seconds\n\nAI Improvements:\n- Fixed AI projectile aiming issues\n- Fixed various bot pathing issues involving towers and crystal capturing\n\nBug Fixes and Improvements:\n- Improved FPS on all Quest devices\n- Fixed an issue which was causing black edges to appear when players turned their head on Quest devices\n- Fixed an bug that could cause players to be kicked off of all queues when 